Task: Address review blockers for Library Visibility & Dashboard (security + date correctness)

Summary:
- Replaced shell-based disk-space execution with argument-safe df execution (`execFile`) to remove command-injection risk from configured root paths.
- Fixed dashboard upcoming movie date selection to choose an in-window release date when one release field is outside the 7-day window.
- Fixed calendar date key/range generation to use local date parts instead of UTC ISO splitting, preventing off-by-one day shifts in non-UTC timezones.
- Updated Recently Added filtering to include `MOVIE_IMPORTED` and `SERIES_IMPORTED` events.
- Added regression tests for all of the above.

Files changed:
- app/src/components/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx
- app/src/components/calendar/dateUtils.ts
- app/src/components/calendar/dateUtils.test.ts
- app/src/components/dashboard/RecentlyAddedWidget.tsx
- app/src/components/dashboard/RecentlyAddedWidget.test.tsx
- server/src/api/routes/dashboardRoutes.ts
- server/src/api/routes/dashboardRoutes.test.ts

Why:
These changes resolve user-visible correctness regressions (calendar day shifts, missing recent imports, incorrect upcoming movie date/status) and remove a security flaw in shell command execution for disk-space checks.
